However, when models and data sets are aligned to specific populations, some are inevitably left behind.
An example of this is that datasets and models are less aligned to non binary people compared to the men and women counterparts.
We find this in the GPT 4 social acceptability task as well as the Dynahate task analysis as well.
So, given that there is positionality in NLP, what can we do about it?
So we have a few recommendations for this.
First one is keep a record of all relevant design choices throughout the research process.
